From c81957233a992d6d5e4fb3870fcc9867b31728ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 07:08:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ussd): feature-phone USSD simulator for live demos

Most smallholders in Rwanda reach services on a 2G feature phone over
USSD, not a smartphone app, so the pitch needs to show that entry point
rather than assert it.

Adds /ussd: a phone frame with a working keypad and a green LCD running a
*789# session - language choice first (English / Kinyarwanda), then sell
produce, market prices, offers with accept/reject, and wallet balance,
ending in a handoff button into the web app.

The session model mirrors a real gateway: resolveScreen is a pure function
of (locale, accumulated input) returning CON to continue or END to close,
so any step can be replayed or rewound mid-presentation, and 0 walks back
a level the way real menus do. Swapping the simulated transport for an
actual gateway would not change the menu code.

The keypad is clickable for stage use and mirrored to the physical
keyboard, so a presenter can drive it without hunting for buttons.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
